part.text:
Now the joda-time UserTypes. I'll create Hibernate 6-compatible UserType implementations in `de.terrestris.shoguncore.hibernate`:

1. `JodaDateTimeUserType implements UserType<ReadableDateTime>`:
```java
public class JodaDateTimeUserType implements UserType<ReadableDateTime> {
    @Override public int getSqlType() { return Types.TIMESTAMP; }  // java.sql.Types.TIMESTAMP
    @Override public Class<ReadableDateTime> returnedClass() { return ReadableDateTime.class; }
    @Override public boolean equals(ReadableDateTime x, ReadableDateTime y) { return Objects.equals(x, y); }
    @Override public int hashCode(ReadableDateTime x) { return x == null ? 0 : x.hashCode(); }
    @Override public ReadableDateTime nullSafeGet(ResultSet rs, int position, SharedSessionContractImplementor session, Object owner) throws SQLException {
        Timestamp timestamp = rs.getTimestamp(position);
        if (rs.wasNull() || timestamp == null) return null;
        return new DateTime(timestamp.getTime());  // hmm — timezone?
    }
    @Override public void nullSafeSet(PreparedStatement st, ReadableDateTime value, int index, SharedSessionContractImplementor session) throws SQLException {
        if (value == null) { st.setNull(index, Types.TIMESTAMP); }
        else { st.setTimestamp(index, new Timestamp(value.getMillis())); }
    }
    @Override public ReadableDateTime deepCopy(ReadableDateTime value) { return value; }  // immutable
    @Override public boolean isMutable() { return false; }
    @Override public Serializable disassemble(ReadableDateTime value) { return value == null ? null : new Timestamp(value.getMillis()); }  hmm — or value itself (ReadableDateTime isn't Serializable? DateTime is Serializable!)
    @Override public ReadableDateTime assemble(Serializable cached, Object owner) { ... }
}
```

Timezone consideration: jadira's PersistentDateTime stored in UTC or local? jadira PersistentDateTime default: TIMESTAMP with... jadira stores DateTime as Timestamp in the JVM default timezone (or UTC depending on configuration). For tests: DateTime.now() → millis; store timestamp = millis (local TZ rendering). Reading back: new DateTime(timestamp.getTime()) — millis preserved → equality via millis ✓. `Restrictions.eq("modified", app3.getModified())` compares millis → TIMESTAMP equality in DB: the stored value must round-trip millis exactly. Timestamp(millis) → H2 TIMESTAMP(6) stores nanos = millis*1e6 ✓ exact. Query param Timestamp(millis) matches stored ✓ (both in same TZ rendering). 

